### Bug : Stale JWT Permissions Assertion in Unit Tests

#### Why it occurs
In `api/auth/login.js` and `api/auth/google.js`, a deliberate architectural/security decision was made **not to bake permissions directly into the JWT token payload**. The code comment states:

> *Only identity claims are embedded in the token. Permissions are intentionally excluded: baking them into a 7-day JWT means a role change (demotion, suspension, permission revocation) cannot take effect until the token naturally expires. Callers that need the current permission set should derive it server-side.*

However, both `tests/loginEndpoint.test.mjs` and the mocked handler in `tests/googleOAuthEndpoint.test.mjs` are stale and still assert that the token contains the `permissions` property:
```javascript
assert.ok(payload.permissions, "JWT should contain permissions");
```
Because the production auth endpoints correctly exclude this claim, these tests fail with an `AssertionError: JWT should contain permissions`.

#### How to fix
1. Remove `permissions` from the simulated token payload inside the mock utility of `tests/googleOAuthEndpoint.test.mjs`.
2. Change the assertions in both test files to expect `payload.permissions` to be `undefined`.

#### Proposed Git Diff

```diff
diff --git a/tests/loginEndpoint.test.mjs b/tests/loginEndpoint.test.mjs
--- a/tests/loginEndpoint.test.mjs
+++ b/tests/loginEndpoint.test.mjs
@@ -243,3 +243,3 @@
   assert.ok(payload.id, "JWT should contain user id");
   assert.ok(payload.email, "JWT should contain email");
   assert.ok(payload.roles, "JWT should contain roles");
-  assert.ok(payload.permissions, "JWT should contain permissions");
+  assert.equal(payload.permissions, undefined, "JWT should NOT contain permissions");
   assert.ok(payload.exp, "JWT should contain expiration");

diff --git a/tests/googleOAuthEndpoint.test.mjs b/tests/googleOAuthEndpoint.test.mjs
--- a/tests/googleOAuthEndpoint.test.mjs
+++ b/tests/googleOAuthEndpoint.test.mjs
@@ -183,3 +183,2 @@
   const roles = user.roles || ["USER"];
   const permissions = getPermissionsForRoles(roles);
   const jwtPayload = {
     id: user.id,
     email: user.email,
     username: user.username,
     roles: roles,
-    permissions: permissions,
     provider: user.provider || "google",
   };
@@ -298,3 +297,3 @@
   assert.ok(payload.id, "JWT should contain user id");
   assert.ok(payload.email, "JWT should contain email");
   assert.ok(payload.roles, "JWT should contain roles");
-  assert.ok(payload.permissions, "JWT should contain permissions");
+  assert.equal(payload.permissions, undefined, "JWT should NOT contain permissions");
   assert.ok(payload.exp, "JWT should contain expiration");

