### Describe the bug

## Bug Description
In `src/components/common/CommandPalette.jsx`, the `query` and 
`activeIndex` states are never reset when the palette closes. If a 
user types a search query, closes the palette, and reopens it, the 
old search term is still present and only filtered results are shown 
instead of the full catalog. The active highlight also retains its 
previous position instead of resetting to the first item.

## Affected File
`src/components/common/CommandPalette.jsx`

## Problematic Code
```js
const [query, setQuery] = useState("");      // ❌ never reset on close
const [activeIndex, setActiveIndex] = useState(0); // ❌ never reset on close

useEffect(() => {
  if (isOpen) {
    setTimeout(() => inputRef.current?.focus(), 150);
    document.body.style.overflow = "hidden";
  } else {
    document.body.style.overflow = ""; // ❌ cleans overflow but NOT query or activeIndex
  }
}, [isOpen]);
```

## Impact
- Palette reopens with stale search query still in the input
- Users see filtered results instead of full catalog on reopen
- Active keyboard highlight retains wrong position
- Poor UX — palette should always open in a clean default state

## Expected Behavior
Every time the palette closes, both `query` and `activeIndex` should 
reset to their initial values so the palette always opens fresh.

## Steps to Reproduce
1. Open Command Palette (Ctrl + K)
2. Type "hackathon" in the search box
3. Close the palette (Esc)
4. Reopen the palette (Ctrl + K)
5. Observe "hackathon" is still in the search box with filtered results

## Suggested Fix
Reset `query` and `activeIndex` in the `else` branch of the `useEffect`:
```js
useEffect(() => {
  if (isOpen) {
    setTimeout(() => inputRef.current?.focus(), 150);
    document.body.style.overflow = "hidden";
  } else {
    document.body.style.overflow = "";
    setQuery("");
    setActiveIndex(0);
  }
}, [isOpen]);
```

## Environment
- File: `src/components/common/CommandPalette.jsx`
- Affects: All users using the Command Palette

