### Describe the bug

## Bug Description
In `src/utils/eventUtils.js`, the `getEventStatus` function always 
returns the date-computed status (`dateStatus`) over the server's 
explicit status (`explicitStatus`). Since `computeDateStatus` always 
returns a truthy string (`"upcoming"`, `"live"`, or `"past"`), the 
condition `if (dateStatus)` is always true — meaning the server's 
explicit status is silently ignored. The final `return explicitStatus || "upcoming"` 
line is completely unreachable dead code.

## Affected File
`src/utils/eventUtils.js`

## Problematic Code
```js
export const getEventStatus = (event) => {
  if (!event) return "upcoming";
  const explicitStatus = mapStatusKey(event.status);
  const dateStatus = computeDateStatus(event);

  if (explicitStatus === "ended") {
    return "ended";
  }
  if (dateStatus) {            // ❌ always true
    return dateStatus;         // ❌ always overrides explicitStatus
  }
  return explicitStatus || "upcoming"; // ❌ dead code — never reached
};
```

## Impact
- Server's explicit event status is always ignored
- An event marked `"live"` by the server but whose date has passed 
  always shows as `"past"` — wrong status displayed to users
- The last return line is dead code — creates false impression of 
  fallback logic that never executes
- Event status badges show incorrect information across all pages

## Expected Behavior
The server's explicit status should take priority over the 
date-computed status when they differ, except for the `"ended"` 
case which is already handled correctly.

## Steps to Reproduce
1. Set an event's explicit status to `"live"` in the data
2. Set its date to a past date
3. Load the Events page
4. Observe the event shows `"past"` instead of `"live"`

## Suggested Fix
```js
export const getEventStatus = (event) => {
  if (!event) return "upcoming";
  const explicitStatus = mapStatusKey(event.status);
  const dateStatus = computeDateStatus(event);

  if (explicitStatus === "ended") {
    return "ended";
  }
  if (explicitStatus && explicitStatus !== dateStatus) {
    return explicitStatus;
  }
  return dateStatus || "upcoming";
};
```

## Environment
- File: `src/utils/eventUtils.js`
- Affects: All event status displays across the app

